=============================================================================
SCOPE NOT TAKEN
=============================================================================

The new HTTP tests prove the PIPELINE, not the business rules. Stock
arithmetic, concurrency, rollback and idempotency are already proven against
the real database at the service layer; re-running them over HTTP would add
running time and no information.

Spec §19's "API tests" row lists a much wider surface — pagination, product,
procurement, receiving, POS, reports. None of those endpoints exist yet.
They arrive with their features in Phase 2 onward, and each brings its own
tests. This card wires the seam; it does not pre-build tests for endpoints
nobody has written.
